# /etc/shadow — Novi Linux.  Mode 0600, root:root.
#
# name:hash:lastchange:min:max:warn:inactive:expire:reserved
#
# An EMPTY hash field means "no password set": login succeeds without
# one. That is what the shipped root entry has, and it is a deliberate
# choice for an installable live image -- the alternative is an image
# nobody can log into. `!` or `*` in that field locks an account.
#
# Set a real password before this machine is anything but a test VM:
#
#     passwd                      # from a console
#     novi-settings               # Account panel, from the desktop
#
# This file is the one thing Novi deliberately keeps OUT of
# /etc/novi/system.conf. system.conf is world-readable and the project
# actively encourages committing it to git; a password hash has no
# business in either. Configuration is declared; secrets are not.
root::19000:0:99999:7:::
nobody:!:19000:0:99999:7:::
